From cb71da74f7b271bada19bc5d3c42179199a8f3e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:38:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] fix-data-6: G-1 359 towns near the big-tech hubs at
 their own place (Bay Area first), K-1 '+ 0% bonus target' is no bonus;
 norm-14

G-1: every place of the 2026-10-16 crawl that geo.js put at its state's or
country's centre, within about 80 km (85 at most) of a city with 200+ big-tech
postings or of Washington, DC, is a '?' gazetteer entry (GeoNames coordinates,
or the town's usual ones). A '?' entry with no region is read with its own
country named, as its own place's name only; a '?' entry never decides what a
two-letter code means. geodiff over all 67,372 location strings: 359 results in
2,206 postings change, latitude and longitude only; 18 move into the SF Bay Area.

K-1: compExtrasEvidence removes a stated 0% bonus target before matching;
relabelJobs clears a stored extras.bonus whose only wording it was (zeroBonusOnly).
Google 2,512 -> 2,462 postings with a bonus mention; every other board unchanged.

norm-14 once for both; golden re-baselined with UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 (2 of 300
hashes, both G-1 towns); refresh fixtures regenerated; version-pinning tests
moved to norm-14; fix-pay-data's 'Dublin, CA' is now a city.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
